        <mxCell id="n112" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#222222;spacing=10;" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• I, Q, IB, QB have an 8UI period; adjacent phases are 2UI apart (only I↔IB and Q↔QB are 4UI apart).&lt;br&gt;• Cells 0/1 use I/IB, so mux[0] and mux[1] switch on I edges. Cells 2/3 use Q/QB, so mux[2] and mux[3] switch 2UI later, as in Fig. 4.&lt;br&gt;• DFF: rising-edge flip-flop. &lt;b&gt;LAT: transparent while EN = 1&lt;/b&gt;; it delays the &quot;0&quot; input by half a period (4UI). MUX: passes input &quot;1&quot; while sel = 1, input &quot;0&quot; otherwise.&lt;br&gt;• Output order: mux[0] = d0, d4, d8, …; mux[1] = d1, d5, …; mux[2] = d2, d6, …; mux[3] = d3, d7, …&lt;br&gt;• Inside the 8:4, each data edge is launched by the same clock edge that ends its selection: ≈4UI of setup-side slack, ≈t&lt;sub&gt;cq&lt;/sub&gt; of hold-side slack.&lt;br&gt;• PI/PD lock drawn with p0/p2 centred on mux[0]/mux[2]; the ~1UI dly re-centres mux[1]/mux[3] (red arrows: 0.5UI → 1.5UI)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="268" width="540" x="20" y="712" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n113" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#444444;" value="t  [UI]" vertex="1">
